From 5fef611a75c274901dc5cc2a350456179e27df7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viljo Marrandi <30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:21:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(ui): light theme gets a light viewport and inks that
 read on it

The 3D pass cleared to a fixed dark colour in every theme. The viewport
ground is now a theme token (light #DDE1E7, dark unchanged), and every
ink drawn over the viewport has a light-ground value tuned on screen:
toolpath moves and boundaries, wireframe, axes, overlays, the view cube
and its buttons (with a centred, symmetric Axes triad), the corner hint
and the playback tool marker.

Unselected paths under "Show all toolpaths" fade toward a light ground
instead of scaling to near-black. Light-theme hover uses the viewport
grey with dark ink, window title bars wear the window fill instead of
egui's dark default, and the Debug info window draws its own title row
whose collapse and close buttons hover like the OS caption buttons.
The dark theme looks as before.

Fixes #698

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
